      "content": "When a school pushes a curriculum, you can look at the specific educational standards they are meeting, not just the political rhetoric surrounding it. If the curriculum is demonstrably tied to established developmental psychology or learning objectives, it suggests a pedagogical basis. However, if the focus is purely on promoting a specific social ideology without clear, measurable educational goals, then it is more likely being driven by political trends than the children's best interests.",
